  "text": {
    "card": "Solve a symbolic ferry puzzle without leaving unsafe token pairs unattended.",
    "puzzle": "puzzle",
    "ferry": "ferry puzzle",
    "crossing": "river crossing puzzle",
    "wrong_configuration": "Choose a crossing offered for the current token configuration; its cargo must share the ferryman bank and leave both banks safe.",
    "hands_empty": "Put down what you hold before changing the puzzle board.",
    "incomplete": "Bring the ferryman and all three symbolic tokens to the far bank before claiming.",
    "already_claimed": "This completed puzzle has already been claimed.",
    "start": "The banks are N (near, left) and F (far, right). The red boat and upright pawn mark the ferryman; W is wolf, G goat and C cabbage. These are symbolic board pieces, not living animals or a transport vehicle. Without the ferryman, wolf cannot share a bank with goat, nor goat with cabbage. Each offered crossing switches ferryman and at most one same-bank token; only safe resulting layouts are offered. Configuration bits on the far bank are ferryman 1, wolf 2, goat 4 and cabbage 8. Start by carrying goat, returning alone, carrying wolf and returning goat.",
    "finish": "After those first four crossings, carry cabbage, return alone, carry goat, then claim the all-far layout for green feedback. Reset returns all pieces to N. State commits at native hand contact; pieces change bank positions discretely. No simulated water, boat trip, living animals, drawn travel or precise individual-piece contact is claimed."
  },
